{"content":[{"c":["BAKBUKIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Shammua’s son, a Levite who assisted Mattaniah at the thanksgiving services in the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.17","r":"Neh.11.17","rawR":"Neh.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.17","value":"Neh.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levite who returned to Jerusalem with Zerubbabel after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.9","r":"Neh.12.9","rawR":"Neh.12.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.9","value":"Neh.12.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of the gatekeepers who had charge of collection centers at the temple gates (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.25","r":"Neh.12.25","rawR":"Neh.12.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.25","value":"Neh.12.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["It is not clear whether these references refer to one, two, or three persons."],"sourceClass":"sp","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bakbukiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 11:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.17","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.17","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.17"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.9","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.9","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.9"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.25","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.25","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9a3e75c9f1526d432a30713f81e7aaa6790c41d918cd4a441df6f1367454c71a","sourceItemName":"Bakbukiah","sourceItemOrder":46,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bakbukiah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary",